  {
   "url": "https://www.boeing.com/content/dam/boeing/v2/airports/acaps/MD80.pdf",
   "title": "Boeing, MD-80 Airplane Characteristics for Airport Planning (Rev. 12/89), 2.2 General Airplane Dimensions: Model MD-81, -82, -83 and -88; 2.7.2 Passenger Entrance and Service Door Clearances",
   "accessed": "2026-11-15",
   "note": "One outline for the MD-81, -82, -83 and -88: the document draws and dimensions them together. Its 2.2 is a 1-bit scan over a printed grid (about 33 px a meter, the grid's lines as thick as the outlines and crossing them), so the fuselage, wing, fin and tailplane are the MD-90's measured lines with its 1.45 m plug ahead of the wing taken out (tools/trace/md82/), checked against this sheet: laid over its views at their scale they fall on its lines within a line's width along the fuselage, wing and tailplane, and the printed figures (45.02 m overall, 32.85 m span, 12.25 m tailplane, 3.35 m width) within 0.4%. Where the two sheets differ the shape keeps the MD-90's vector drawing of the same tail: the MD-80 scan draws the tail cone's underside up to 0.35 m higher and the fin's leading edge about 0.3 m further forward. This sheet's own: the JT8D-200 nacelle (side view; its inlet and stub pylon in the front view, 2.70 m from the centerline as printed, where the plan draws it at 2.62 m), the pylon in the plan, and the doors' and cabin windows' places along the body (the side view, at the printed 41.58 m from the nose to the tail cone). The main entry door sits within 2 cm of 2.7.2's printed 4.38 m to its middle; the right side's service door is placed from 2.7.2's partial plan (27 in wide, 48.5 in tall, 4.51 m to its middle, its sill with the main door's). The scan draws every door 0.1-0.2 m higher on the tube than the MD-90's vector sheet and 2.7.2's section (its door sill 0.53 m below the centerline), so the doors' and windows' heights are the MD-90 sheet's. The side view draws the tube 1.4% short of the printed 3.61 m and the MD-90's 3.6% tall: the fuselage is fit to the printed height (fit_height.py). Confidence medium: the scan, and the tail's two drawings."
  },
  {
   "url": "https://www.boeing.com/content/dam/boeing/v2/airports/acaps/MD90.pdf",
   "title": "Boeing, MD-90-30/-30ER Airplane Characteristics for Airport Planning (MDC K9099, October 2002), 2.2 General Airplane Dimensions, 2.3 Ground Clearances",
   "accessed": "2026-11-15",
   "note": "The fuselage, wing, fin and tailplane, as measured for the MD-90 (shapes/MD90.json), with its 1.45 m stretch ahead of the wing taken out: the MD-90 is the MD-80's airframe with that plug (the two documents' fuselage lengths, 43.03 m and 41.58 m, and wheelbases, 23.52 m and 22.05 m, differ by it)."
  }
